{"base":"92981bf2909d564fc94631fa95c8d1eb4dbe1ed4","description":"- rename the COB-facing `add` command to `register`; keep `add` as a\n  hidden alias so existing scripts keep working\n- rename internal symbols to match (Command::Register,\n  register_artifact, error::Register)\n- spell out in help text that registering records signed discovery\n  metadata, not bytes\n\nDistinguishes registering release metadata from seeding the bytes, so\nthe two layers read distinctly across the CLI.\n\n\nrefactor: rename AddArtifact to RegisterArtifact\n\n- rename the Action variant and the add_artifact methods to\n  register_artifact, matching the CLI `register` command\n- pin the serialized action name to `AddArtifact` via serde(rename) so\n  COBs written before the rename still deserialize\n- add a test locking the legacy wire tag\n- update the call site in the CLI\n\nKeeps the library vocabulary consistent with the renamed command while\npreserving on-the-wire backward compatibility for existing COBs.\n\n\ndocs: clarify register vs seed distinction\n\n- contrast registering (signed COB metadata, synced over radicle) with\n  seeding (a node serving bytes over iroh) in CONTEXT.md\n- add Register and Seed verb entries; replace \"serving\" with \"seeding\"\n- update README workflow step and command list for the rename\n\nSharpens the vocabulary so the metadata layer and the byte-serving\nlayer are not conflated.\n\n\ndocs(changelog): note add to register rename\n\n- record the `add` → `register` rename under Unreleased\n- flag it as a breaking API change for library consumers\n  (Release::register_artifact, Action::RegisterArtifact)\n- clarify the CLI alias and serde-pinned wire format mean no script\n  breakage and no COB migration\n\nSets expectations for crate consumers upgrading across the rename.","oid":"21987a40c7ea633f1bdcf34256063e915228658e","type":"revision"}